    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze this document and classify it.\n\n### Original Filename:\n{{ $json.document.original_file_name }}\n\n### Created:\n{{ $json.document.created }}\n\n### Title:\n{{ $json.document.title }}\n\n### Content:\n{{ $json.document.content }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are a document analysis AI for a multilingual user.\nDocuments may be in English, Portuguese (Brazil), or Polish.\n\nYour task is to extract structured metadata for document classification.\n\nFIELD RULES:\n\n1) tags\n- Choose ONLY from the list below.\n- Return tags in lowercase exactly as shown.\n- You may return MULTIPLE tags when applicable.\n- Return an empty array if no tag applies.\n\nALLOWED TAGS:\n{{ Object.keys($json.tagMap).join(', ') }}\n\n2) correspondent\n- The organization that ISSUED or SENT this document (not the recipient).\n- Look for: letterhead, logo, header, sender address, signature block, URLs, email domains, copyright notices.\n- IMPORTANT: Only use an existing correspondent if the name genuinely matches the document's issuer. Do NOT default to existing entries just because the list is short.\n- If the issuer is not in the existing list, return the organization name exactly as written in the document (do NOT translate).\n- Return null only if the document has no identifiable issuing organization.\n\nEXISTING CORRESPONDENTS (use only if genuinely matching):\n{{ Object.values($json.correspondentMap).map(c => c.name).slice(0,300).join(', ') || 'none yet' }}\n\n3) document_type\n- Choose from the existing list below OR one of the canonical types.\n- Return in lowercase.\n- Return null if nothing fits.\n\nEXISTING DOCUMENT TYPES:\n{{ Object.keys($json.documentTypeMap).slice(0,100).join(', ') || 'none yet' }}\n\nCANONICAL TYPES (use lowercase):\ninvoice, receipt, contract, statement, letter, certificate, report, form, notification, id document, medical record, insurance document, tax document, legal document, utility bill, bank statement, payslip, ticket, warranty, manual\n\n4) title\n- Concise, descriptive title in English (translate if needed).\n- Maximum 80 characters.\n\n5) date\n- Primary document date (issue date, not due date) in YYYY-MM-DD format.\n- Return null if no date found."
